{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"052b1eb7","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.007828,"end_time":"2026-11-25T21:33:10.227737+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-25T21:33:10.219909+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# Numerai Classic v6.0 (\"Unity\") — MiniRocket Regressor (`NumeraiExtractions` + `MiniRocketNumeraiEstimator`)\n","\n","- **Data Loading (`data_utils.load_unity_numerai_data_cached`)**: Resolves and downloads the Unity v6.0 Parquets using the official Kaggle clients (`kagglehub.dataset_download` and `kaggle.api.kaggle_api_extended.KaggleApi`) with `numerapi.NumerAPI` fallback, caches processed Parquets, and supports independent training & validation downsampling (`downsample_mode`/`downsample_frac` and `val_downsample_mode`/`val_downsample_frac`).\n","- **Exploratory Data Analysis (`# EDA`)**: Lists available `TARGET_COL` and `feature_set` options from `features.json`, inspects `train_df.head(2)` / `validation_df.head(2)` and `info()`, plots era sizes over time, overlays feature standard-deviation distributions across Train vs. Validation, and displays the top 10 features correlated with `TARGET_COL` along with ADF stationarity checks.\n","\n","---\n","\n","### 1. Feature Extraction Parameters (`utils.NumeraiExtractions` — `estimator__extractor__*`)\n","- Shared across `baseline_unity.ipynb`, `lightgbm_unity.ipynb`, and `minirocket_unity.ipynb` (correlation ranking, variance filtering, sparse selection, PCA, cross-sectional quantization, rolling-era & lag-diff statistics, per-ticker time-series features, and Fourier harmonics).\n","\n","---\n","\n","### 2. Shared Parent Estimator Parameters (`baseline_utils.BaseNumeraiEstimator` — `estimator__*`)\n","- **`correlation_method`** (`[None, 'pandas_mean', 'numerai_mean', 'pearson', 'spearman']`): How the estimator scores post-extraction features against `TARGET_COL` (used when `top_k` is set).\n","- **`abs_corr`** (`[True, False]`): `True` selects top features by $|\\text{corr}|$; `False` selects by signed $\\text{corr}$.\n","- **`top_k`** (`[None, 20, 40, 80]`): Number of top post-extraction features passed to MiniRocket (`None` uses all extracted features).\n","- **`era_weighting`** (`[None, 'equal_era', 'recency_linear', 'recency_exp']`): Computes per-row `sample_weight` passed into the linear head (`None`, equal weight per era, linear recency, or exponential recency decay).\n","- **`recency_decay`** (`Real(0.001, 0.020)`): Exponential decay rate per era when `era_weighting='recency_exp'`.\n","- **`prediction_transform`** (`[None, 'era_zscore', 'era_rank']`): Post-prediction within-era normalization (`None` = raw, `'era_zscore'`, or `'era_rank'`).\n","- **`bias_correction`** (`[None, 'mean_residual']`): When `'mean_residual'`, records `mean(y_train - y_hat_train)` in `fit()` and adds it to predictions in `predict()` (`None` disables).\n","- **Walk-Forward & Horizon Controls**: `walk_forward_step_eras`, `walk_forward_window`, `target_horizon_eras`, `era_stride`.\n","\n","---\n","\n","### 3. MiniRocket Model Parameters (`minirocket_utils.MiniRocketNumeraiEstimator` — `estimator__*`)\n","- **Sequence Construction**:\n","  - **`input_mode`** (`['ticker_sequence', 'feature_profile']`): `'ticker_sequence'` constructs a strictly causal multivariate `(C, seq_len)` sequence per `numerai_ticker` with a training tail buffer for leak-free validation warm-up; `'feature_profile'` applies univariate MiniRocket across each row's feature vector.\n","  - **`seq_len`** (`[9, 12, 16, 24]`): Causal lookback window length in eras (minimum `9` to match MiniRocket's length-9 kernels).\n","  - **`max_channels`** (`[8, 16, 32]`): Maximum top-ranked feature channels fed into multivariate MiniRocket.\n","  - **`pad_mode`** (`['first', 'neutral']`): Left-padding strategy for tickers with fewer than `seq_len` historical eras (`'first'` repeats earliest value; `'neutral'` pads with `2.0`).\n","- **MiniRocket Kernel & Dilation Bank (Dempster et al., 2021)**:\n","  - **`num_kernels`** (`[420, 840, 1680, 3360]`): Number of PPV features (rounded to a multiple of the 84 fixed length-9 `{-1, +2}` kernels).\n","  - **`max_dilations_per_kernel`** (`[4, 8, 16, 32]`): Maximum exponentially spaced dilations per base kernel.\n","  - **`fit_sample_size`** (`[1024, 2048, 4096]`): Training subsample size used to draw quantile biases.\n","  - **`backend`** (`['numpy', 'sktime', 'auto']`): Pure-NumPy vectorized Dempster-2021 MiniRocket (`'numpy'`, zero JIT cold-start & Kaggle-portable) or `sktime` Numba backend (`'sktime'` / `'auto'`).\n","- **OOM-Proof Batched Linear Head**:\n","  - **`standardize_features`** (`[True, False]`): Standardizes PPV features before fitting the linear head.\n","  - **`head_type`** (`['ridge_cv', 'ridge', 'sgd_elasticnet', 'sgd_huber']`): Single-pass batched analytical Ridge / RidgeCV (GCV) or batched SGD head (`elasticnet` / `huber`) — never materializes `(N, num_kernels)` in RAM.\n","  - **`alpha`** (`[1.0, 10.0, 100.0, 1000.0]` / `Real(1e-2, 1e5, prior='log-uniform')`): Regularization strength for `'ridge'` / SGD heads.\n","  - **`l1_ratio`** (`[0.05, 0.15, 0.5]` / `Real(0.0, 1.0)`): ElasticNet mixing parameter (active when `head_type='sgd_elasticnet'`).\n","  - **`huber_epsilon`** (`[1.1, 1.35, 1.75]` / `Real(1.05, 2.5)`): Huber outlier threshold (active when `head_type='sgd_huber'`).\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"c05f072c","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-25T21:33:10.246594Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-25T21:33:10.245907Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-25T21:33:22.912308Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-25T21:33:22.911185Z"},"papermill":{"duration":12.676365,"end_time":"2026-11-25T21:33:22.914393+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-25T21:33:10.238028+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Warning: Looks like you're using an outdated `kaggle` version (installed: 2.0.2), please consider upgradi